                        <field name="dc_description">In the period between 1875 and 1900 the Wilhelminian architectural style shaped the railway architecture. From 1910 the more objective “Werkbund style” followed. A good example of this is the railway station of Mülheim am Rhein (now Cologne - Mülheim) in Leipzig. The railway station is situated between Cologne and Düsseldorf and was built in 1908. The architects were Mettegang and Müller von der Kgl. Cologne Railway Directorate. The building was destroyed during World War II. The model dates back to construction time.<br/>
<br/>
VtW 1909, H. 47, p. 755ff <br/>
Bahn & Model 2 Jg., October 1988, H. 10, p. 71f (Fig. Model) (Deutsches Technikmuseum) </field>
